---
/**
 * About page (IDENT-04 + PROJ-03 folded — D-08, D-03, D-21).
 *
 * Thesis-first, bio-second. Per D-08 the two halves are fused on one page:
 * the WHY (Cross The Bridge doctrine — Money/Data/Infrastructure pillars,
 * distilled from petros-polaris.md Page 1) before the WHO (Wesley's voice
 * + style + what he's currently building, distilled from About Me.md).
 *
 * D-21 (locked 2026-04-27): canonical name is "Wesley Schlemmer". The H1
 * label stays "About Wesley" (first-name only is fine for a heading);
 * the JSON-LD Person schema emitted via BaseLayout's JsonLd component
 * carries the full canonical name.
 *
 * Voice contract honored (UI-SPEC §Copywriting + RESEARCH PITFALLS #2):
 *   - Zero doctrine words from the vault (the four banned phrases are
 *     enumerated in 01-UI-SPEC.md §Copywriting voice contract).
 *   - Zero product detail for the deferred AI/Petros productization —
 *     that depth lives on the future CTB brand site, not this About
 *     page (D-08 + CONTEXT.md <deferred>).
 *   - Zero marketing-ese (the five banned terms enumerated in
 *     01-UI-SPEC.md §Copywriting voice contract).
 *   - The brand line appears exactly once, in the closing sentence of
 *     the thesis.
 *
 * h-card microformats (RESEARCH §h-card lines 1133-1146; SEO-06 hedge
 * shipped in Phase 1 even though SEO-06 is mapped to Phase 2):
 *   - Article container: class="h-card"
 *   - H1: class="p-name"
 *   - Role line: class="p-job-title" containing class="u-url" → link to
 *     https://crossthebridge.io (the CTB brand domain — D-05 revised;
 *     intentional, NOT a stale wesleyschlemmer.com swap target)
 *   - Headshot wrapped in div.u-photo so the Astro <Image> emits valid
 *     u-photo markup at indiewebify.me
 *
 * Body copy authored by Claude under the autonomous-bypass authorization
 * for this plan (mirror of 01-09 CTB teaser pattern). Drafts pre-existed
 * at .planning/phases/01-foundation-personal-surface/01-08-DRAFT.md.
 * Wesley reviews + edits in a follow-up plan post-launch.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Headshot from '../components/Headshot.astro';

const title = 'About';
const description =
  "Wesley Schlemmer's bio fused with the Cross The Bridge thesis — Bitcoin, sovereign AI, Freedom Tech, and the work of opting out of legacy systems.";
const canonical = '/about';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLdSchema="person"
>
  <article class="about h-card" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Person">
    <header class="about__header">
      <h1 class="about__h1 p-name" itemprop="name">About Wesley</h1>
      <p class="about__role p-job-title">
        <span itemprop="jobTitle">Founder</span>,
        <a class="u-url" href="https://crossthebridge.io" itemprop="url">Cross The Bridge</a>
      </p>
      <hr class="about__rule" aria-hidden="true" />
    </header>

    <div class="about__layout">
      <aside class="about__headshot">
        {/* Astro <Image /> emits an <img>; the wrapper div carries
            class="u-photo" so the markup validates at indiewebify.me. */}
        <div class="u-photo">
          <Headshot />
        </div>
      </aside>

      <div class="about__content">
        <section class="about__thesis">
          <h2 class="about__h2">The Thesis: Cross The Bridge</h2>
          <p>
            The internet I grew up on rewarded curiosity. The one we have now treats
            people as a behavioral surface to be measured, monetized, and steered.
            Money flows through systems built to surveil. Data is collected, sold,
            and weaponized. Infrastructure is centralized to a handful of vendors
            that can revoke access at will. None of this requires a conspiracy to
            explain — the incentives are already pointed in that direction.
          </p>
          <p>
            The work I do is organized around three pillars. <strong>Money:</strong>
            Bitcoin and Monero return monetary control to the people holding the
            keys, not the institutions issuing the rails. <strong>Data:</strong>
            open-source tools, encryption, and self-hosting let people retain what
            gets recorded about them. <strong>Infrastructure:</strong> owning the
            nodes, the compute, and the storage that mediate daily life — instead
            of renting them — is the framework I want to leave my kids.
          </p>
          <p>
            None of these are new ideas on their own. Stitched together, they're a
            path. The point of the work: <em>Cross the bridge from the Old World to the New</em>.
            Leave the legacy systems behind and build what comes next, deliberately,
            while it's still possible to opt out without going off-grid.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="about__bio">
          <h2 class="about__h2">About Me</h2>

          <h3>My Style</h3>
          <p>
            Everything, everywhere, all at once. I run multiple projects in parallel
            and hate wasted time — engineer's habit. I'd rather double-dip than
            focus, which means I'm at my best at the strategy level: pulling
            threads together, spotting where two unrelated problems share a
            solution, picking the team that can ship. The trade-off is the
            day-to-day. Small details, scheduling, repeating myself — those are
            where I leak time. I try to delegate or automate them; sometimes I
            get away with it.
          </p>

          <h3>How I Work</h3>
          <p>
            I work in waves. There are stretches where I'm head-down on one
            deadline well into the night, and stretches of unstructured time
            where I'm reading, writing, or talking to people in the same orbit.
            I'm rarely fully off, and I'd rather take a Tuesday afternoon with
            the family than punch in for a 9-to-5. Most useful things I've
            built started as a conversation. So I keep the calendar light
            enough to have those conversations, and the phone off enough to
            actually finish what they generate.
          </p>

          <h3>What I'm Building</h3>
          <p>
            Right now: <a href="/projects/bitcoin-bay">Bitcoin Bay</a>, the
            Florida-Bitcoin community I helped build.
            <a href="/projects/fbba">FBBA</a>, shaping the state-level policy
            edge. <a href="/projects/cross-the-bridge">Cross The Bridge</a>,
            the brand for the consulting work — AI implementation, agent
            integration, and the sovereign-AI stack this thesis points at —
            paid work for Tampa Bay teams putting AI to actual use, which
            funds the rest. The bridge isn't a hypothetical; it's the thing
            being built.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: var(--measure-wide);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--spacing-3xl) var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-4xl);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about { padding: var(--spacing-3xl) var(--spacing-2xl) var(--spacing-4xl); }
  }

  .about__header { margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl); }
  .about__h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: var(--leading-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md) 0;
  }
  .about__role {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-charcoal-mid);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-lg) 0;
  }
  .about__role .u-url {
    color: var(--color-green);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .about__role .u-url:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .about__role .u-url:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-green);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .about__rule {
    border: 0;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--color-gold);
    width: 80px;
    margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0 0;
  }

  .about__layout {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about__layout {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 280px;
      gap: var(--spacing-2xl);
      align-items: start;
    }
    .about__headshot { order: 2; }
    .about__content { order: 1; }
  }

  .about__h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: var(--leading-heading);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md) 0;
  }
  .about__thesis,
  .about__bio { margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl); }
  .about__thesis p,
  .about__bio p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md) 0;
  }
  .about__thesis strong { color: var(--color-charcoal); font-weight: 700; }
  .about__thesis em {
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .about__bio h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0 var(--spacing-sm) 0;
  }
  .about__bio a,
  .about__thesis a {
    color: var(--color-green);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .about__bio a:hover,
  .about__thesis a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .about__bio a:focus-visible,
  .about__thesis a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-green);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
